From: Omarchy Mobile <omamobile@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: msm8953-xiaomi-markw: route the speaker amplifier

The AW8738 loudspeaker amplifier is an aux device of the sound card,
but no route connects its input to the codec, so DAPM treats it as an
always-on path and keeps the amplifier's enable GPIO driven whether or
not anything plays.

On a Redmi 4 Prime the amplifier is fed from the PM8953 codec's line
output: with "RX3 MIX1 INP1" set to RX1 and the LINEOUT and LINEOUT Ext
switches on, a tone from MultiMedia1 plays on the loudspeaker, while
the SPK DAC path and the HPHR path stay silent (each tested alone).
Route the amplifier's input from LINEOUT_OUT, so it is powered only
while the line output is.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8953-xiaomi-markw.dts
@@ -302,7 +302,8 @@
 		"MM_DL1", "MultiMedia1 Playback",
 		"MM_DL3", "MultiMedia3 Playback",
 		"MM_DL4", "MultiMedia4 Playback",
-		"MultiMedia2 Capture", "MM_UL2";
+		"MultiMedia2 Capture", "MM_UL2",
+		"Speaker Amp IN", "LINEOUT_OUT";
 
 	pinctrl-0 = <&cdc_pdm_lines_default
 		     &cdc_pdm_lines_2_default
